WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.736 --> 00:00:02.411
- [Narrator] Nothing
in Portugal stands out

00:00:02.411 --> 00:00:04.087
quite like the vibrant colors

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:07.337
and unusual architecture of Pena Place.

00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:14.592
Pena National Palace is located

00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:18.057
within western Portugal Sintra Mountains.

00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:20.469
Although the palace's very design touches

00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:22.426
make it appear as though it has been built

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:25.114
from multiple pieces of different castles,

00:00:25.114 --> 00:00:28.152
the building's unusual style
is the result of an owner

00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:30.902
with extremely flamboyant tastes.

00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:35.379
The palace was owned by King Ferdinand II,

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:37.512
who built it to serve as a summer home

00:00:37.512 --> 00:00:40.932
for Portuguese royals in
the late 18th century.

00:00:40.932 --> 00:00:43.907
The castle itself is built
around an old monastery,

00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:45.652
and is made up of colored sections,

00:00:45.652 --> 00:00:49.334
including a red clock
tower and a yellow minaret.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.388
During the revolution
of 1910, the royals fled

00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:55.305
and the palace and its
grounds were abandoned.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:57.079
It wasn't until the 20th century

00:00:57.079 --> 00:00:58.863
that it was restored by the state

00:00:58.863 --> 00:01:02.487
and earned itself a UNESCO
Heritage Site designation.

00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:04.808
King Ferdinand's wide ranging tastes

00:01:04.808 --> 00:01:07.113
have made Pena Palace a microcosm

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:09.101
for all the styles of architecture

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.018
the world has to offer.

